  "card": "Standardizes the network classification of linked-IPv4 addresses (such as 6to4 and Teredo) across AddrMan filtering and RPC endpoints. Previously, AddrMan size tracking and getaddrmaninfo counted these addresses as IPv6, while AddrMan address retrieval filtering and labels in getnodeaddresses and getrawaddrman treated them as IPv4, causing filter mismatches and assertion failures in fuzz tests. The change updates GetAddr_() and the RPCs to use GetNetwork() instead of GetNetClass(), keeping GetNetClass() strictly for bucketing decisions.",
